  "config_guidance": {
    "session.upload_progress.enabled": "PHP's own guidance for CVE-2026-109619 and the still-unpatched CVE-2026-115560: set to 0 (Off) in php.ini or pool config and restart workers. ini_set() and display_errors hiding are NOT sufficient.",
    "memory_limit": "A finite memory_limit is the soft-limit OOM trigger surface for CVE-2026-109618. PHP's temporary mitigation is memory_limit=-1 applied non-overridably (php_admin_value), trading DoS exposure for removing the PHP-level OOM path. cgroup/container limits are the safe way to bound memory; never use RLIMIT_AS/RLIMIT_DATA/RLimitMEM.",
    "post_max_size": "Keep small (8M without uploads, ~32M with). Note: post_max_size is enforced against the declared Content-Length only; chunked/HTTP2 lengthless bodies and decompressing proxies bypass it.",
    "fatal_error_backtraces": "PHP 8.5 only: PHP advises setting fatal_error_backtraces=0 until fixed (relates to CVE-2026-109619 handling).",
    "session.serialize_handler": "CVE-2026-115560: configuring session.serialize_handler=php_binary or php_serialize in INI and switching to 'php' via ini_set() before session_start() is the vulnerable pattern. Disabling session.upload_progress removes this surface until the fix ships."
